<title>SPAIN: Popular sets up consumer loan joint venture.</title>
<headline>Popular sets up consumer loan joint venture.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-02-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spain's Banco Popular said on Tuesday it was setting up a 50-50 joint venture with Cofinoga, a unit of the Galeries Lafayette group, to finance consumer credit.</p>
<p>The joint venture has capital of 1.5 billion pesetas, Popular said.  </p>
<p>Popular said the new affiliate will distribute private credit cards for retail chains, provide loans from retail outlets as well as personal consumer loans via direct marketing.</p>
<p>The bank said the deal was part of its policy to seek international alliances and develop new business activity areas.</p>
<p>-- Madrid newsroom +341 585 2160</p>
